---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectCard from "../components/ProjectCard.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Matthew Ralph — AI Transformation & Business Systems" description="AI transformation, technical-program leadership, and business-systems work focused on governed workflows and operational execution.">
  <section class="hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">Portfolio</p><h1>Matthew Ralph</h1><p class="lead">Business systems and AI transformation operator focused on governed workflows, technical-program direction, and operational systems.</p><p class="role-focus">Focused on AI transformation, technical-program leadership, and business-systems roles where governance, workflow design, and operational execution matter.</p><p class="hero-actions"><a class="text-link" href="#selected-work">Explore systems <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/salessuccess/">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples">Public work samples <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p></section>
  <section class="commercial-foundation shell" aria-labelledby="commercial-foundation-title"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Commercial foundation</p><h2 id="commercial-foundation-title">Commercial operator first. Systems work built on top.</h2></div><p class="commercial-intro">15+ years across commercial leadership, GTM, enablement, business development, client operations, and business-building inform Matthew’s current work in governed systems and AI transformation.</p><div class="commercial-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">Enablement program outcome</p><strong>40% conversion improvement</strong><span>Contributed to a broader enablement program that improved conversion by 40% and reduced ramp time by 30%.</span></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Commercial scale</p><strong>$2.5M+ quarterly pipeline</strong><span>Supported $2.5M+ in quarterly pipeline through disciplined commercial process and performance visibility.</span></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Direct execution</p><strong>$2M+ recurring revenue</strong><span>Generated $2M+ in recurring revenue while increasing average deal size by 35%.</span></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Operating leadership</p><strong>56 employees · ~90% retention</strong><span>Co-founded and scaled Right Choice Security to 56 employees while maintaining approximately 90% client retention.</span></article></div></section>
  <section class="shell work-section" aria-labelledby="selected-work"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><h2 id="selected-work">Two governed systems for consequential work.</h2></div><div class="project-grid"><ProjectCard title="Job Opportunity Engine" label="AI systems & governance" description="Private, local-first job collection, evaluation, and review-oriented preparation with governed evidence and human authority." href={`${base}/work/job-opportunity-engine/`} /><ProjectCard title="Response Flow Systems" label="Implemented offline governance" description="Outbound approval, evidence custody, message lineage, and fail-closed exception handling for commercial workflows." href={`${base}/work/response-flow-systems/`} /></div><p class="work-samples-note">Looking for architecture and governance documentation? <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples">Inspect public work samples <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p></section>
  <section class="shell pir-proof" aria-labelledby="pir-proof-title"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Strong secondary system</p><h2 id="pir-proof-title">A governed refinery between untrusted material and durable claims.</h2></div><article class="pir-proof-card"><div><p class="eyebrow">Personal Intelligence Refinery</p><h3>AI-assisted research with deterministic validation and human authority.</h3><p>Model proposals cannot become durable truth without exact grounding, deterministic validation, and an explicit human decision.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>5 / 5 frozen expected spans</dd></div><div><dt>Grounding</dt><dd>0 violations</dd></div><div><dt>Human authority</dt><dd>5 ACCEPT / 1 REJECT</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href={`${base}/work/personal-intelligence-refinery/`}>Inspect PIR <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></section>
  <section class="shell lab-proof" aria-labelledby="lab-proof-title"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Focused technical proof</p><h2 id="lab-proof-title">AI evaluation requires judgment about the evaluator, too.</h2></div><article class="lab-proof-card"><div><p class="eyebrow">AI Systems Reliability Lab · Lab 01</p><h3>Model Regression Gate</h3><p>A frozen, synthetic experiment comparing two AI configurations across 30 cases—then auditing whether the semantic evaluator had earned release authority.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Release gate</dt><dd>FAIL</dd></div><div><dt>Human audit</dt><dd>60 / 60 outputs</dd></div><div><dt>Finding</dt><dd>Evaluator authority challenged</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href={`${base}/work/ai-systems-reliability-lab/`}>Inspect the Lab <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
